# omabackup allowlist (seed list)
#
# Paths under $HOME that omabackup backs up, one per line, relative to $HOME.
# Directories are copied recursively. Globs are expanded by the shell. Lines
# starting with # are comments.
#
# A leading '?' marks an entry optional: a missing optional entry is skipped
# and reported as gone instead of halting the run. A required entry (no
# leading '?') that does not resolve halts the snapshot by design, and no two
# Omarchy machines carry the exact same set of stock files, so every entry
# below ships marked optional. Once you have confirmed a path exists on your
# machine and want a missing copy to stop the backup instead of just being
# noted, drop its '?'.
#
# Anything not listed here is never backed up; the drift verb reports what is
# missing.

# --- Hyprland ---
?.config/hypr

# --- Omarchy: the desktop's identity ---
?.config/omarchy/themebook.json
?.config/omarchy/shell.json
?.config/omarchy/shell.toml
?.config/omarchy/displays.json
?.config/omarchy/dock.json
?.config/omarchy/defaults
?.config/omarchy/hooks
?.config/omarchy/themes
?.config/omarchy/extensions
?.config/omarchy/branding

# --- Terminals ---
?.config/alacritty
?.config/foot
?.config/ghostty
?.config/kitty

# --- Shell / prompt / TUI ---
?.bashrc
?.bash_profile
?.XCompose
?.config/starship.toml
?.config/btop
?.config/tmux
?.config/autostart
?.config/chromium-flags.conf

# --- Deliberately excluded (do not add without reading lib/drift.sh) ---
#   .ssh/                        private key
#   .config/gh/hosts.yml         OAuth token
#   .config/wireguard/           live PrivateKey= values
#   .local/state/syncthing/      key.pem, https-key.pem, API key
#   .config/omarchy/plugins/     third-party plugin clones, treated as regenerable
#   .config/Code/User/globalStorage, workspaceStorage   credentials
#   dconf/user (binary)          captured as manifests/dconf.txt instead
